title: AutoGen silently drops properties whose $ref does not resolve
updated: 2026-08-18T17:47:47Z
---

lib/IO/K8s/AutoGen.pm:249 (return undef) + :176 (next unless defined
$type_spec) -- a property referencing a definition missing from all_defs
is simply never turned into an attribute. Moo ignores unknown
constructor arguments, so inflation ACCEPTS the data and TO_JSON never
emits it again. No error, no warning: silent data loss on the roundtrip.

Repro (measured): spec => { "\$ref" => "#/definitions/...MissingDef" },
inflate with spec => { important => "data" } -- object builds,
can("spec") is false, TO_JSON has no spec key.

Fix sketch: fall back to an opaque { Str => 1 } attribute instead of
skipping, or at minimum warn/croak naming class + field. Fail-closed is
the house line (karr #37/#39): silent acceptance-then-loss is the worst
of the options.

Found in the 2026-08-18 core-module review (repro verified).
Lane: io-k8s-worker, then io-k8s-test-writer (t/04_autogen.t).
